explanation:
Since the condition depends on vertical ordering, we examine the array column by column instead of row by row.
For each column, we compare every pair of adjacent strings to check whether characters are in non-decreasing order.
If we find any character that is greater than the character below it, that column violates sorting rules.
Such a column must be deleted, so we increase the count and move to the next column.
After checking all columns, the total count gives the minimum deletions required.
code:
class Solution {
    public int minDeletionSize(String[] strs) {
        int rows=strs.length;
        int cols=strs[0].length();
        int count=0;
        for(int col=0;col<cols;col++){
            for(int row=0;row<rows-1;row++){
                if(strs[row].charAt(col)>strs[row+1].charAt(col)){
                    count++;
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
}
